PlasmaDX Workspace Rules (Context Seed)

- Project: PlasmaDX - DirectX 12 + DXR 1.2 (SER). Central feature is ray-traced lighting (self-shadowing next). Keep RT lighting working across all modes.
- Demo goal: First-person, sweeping spotlight in a dark scene; primitive toggle (sphere/cube); yellow background safeguard toggle; WASD + mouse.

Key Files
- src/core/App.cpp, App.h - app init, input, DXR dispatch, toggles, FPS
- src/dxr/SBT.cpp - real SBT (aligned records; shader identifiers)
- src/dxr/ASBuilder.cpp - BLAS/TLAS build
- shaders/dxr/raytracing_lib.hlsl - raygen/miss/closesthit, camera rays, spotlight volumetric demo, blend
- shaders/vol/ray_march_cs.hlsl - volumetric ray march; anisotropy g
- src/volumetric/MetaballSystem.* - metaballs (optional volumetric mode)

Runtime Env Toggles (set before launching PlasmaDX.exe)
- PLASMADX_DISABLE_DXR: "0" enable, "1" disable
- PLASMADX_DEBUG_MODE: e.g. "3" for cube-in-dark torch demo
- PLASMADX_DXR_BLEND: "0|1" toggle additive blend with raster/compute
- PLASMADX_NO_DEBUG: "1" suppress extra logs/UI
- PLASMADX_NO_QUIT_ON_REMOVAL: "1" keep app alive if device lost

Input Controls
- WASD: move; mouse: look
- F: attach/detach torch to camera
- C: cycle light colors
- P / O: increase / decrease metaball count (when enabled)
- 5 / 6: adjust anisotropy g
- B: toggle DXR blend
- N / M: adjust blend scale

DXR Pipeline Expectations
- Root signature: TLAS SRV (t0), HDR UAV descriptor table (u0), GlobalParams root constants (b0)
- Ensure SBT record alignment; SRV/UAV heaps bound before DispatchRays; correct barriers around HDR UAV and Present

Agent Guidance
- Do not remove DXR lighting during refactors; keep a working RT path or add a runtime toggle
- Prefer non-destructive, localized, readable edits
- If adding modes, wire via GlobalParams and expose simple hotkeys

WSL Remote Tip
- Opening a WSL Remote window creates a new chat. To retain context, open the same workspace path via /mnt/d/... so the same .cursor folder is used, and keep this rules file present. If chat resets, paste the seed below into your first WSL message.

